  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Pass and defend – the passer becomes the back in a 2 v 1",
  "description": "One goal with a goalkeeper, three lines at the centre line (A by the left board, B in the middle with the balls, C by the right board) and a cone out in front of goal on C's side. C sprints without the ball and rounds the cone. At the same time B carries the ball a few steps and passes to C. Straight after the pass, B races down in front of goal and plays as the defender, while A runs down towards goal on the other side.\n\nNow it is 2 v 1: C shoots or passes to A, who shoots. Whichever of A and C does not shoot follows up for the rebound. Switch lines after each turn: A to B, B to C and C to A. Run it just as much mirrored. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Time the starts so nobody has to wait for the ball – everything happens at speed."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "B: pass and go at once – take the shortest way back to the slot."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "C: take on the defender and decide late – shoot if they cover A, pass if they come at you."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "The defender closes the shooting lane and reads the pass across to A."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
